Yeah, yeah.  I know all this.  For the YANI post, I purposely ignored
it.

Here is the thing.  I don't LIKE coming up with items based on their
place in the current game.  For a long time Nethack's cool stuff was
just added in because they were cool and useful in a general dungeon
exploration game.  It was only later that they were all shoehorned
into a kinda-sorta design, and perhaps not coincidentally, that's
about when Devteam work on the game slowed down tremendously.  Many of
the things I like in Nethack are holdovers from Rogue.  I think the
game could stand to return to that idea.


